      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Image to Depth (Iris-Z small)",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Image to Depth (Iris-Z small)\n\nA depth map of a photo. Iris-Z small is FLUX.2 Klein base 9B trained to make pictures and their depth maps\ntogether; here it is given the photo and draws only the depth, in 4 steps, without a prompt or text encoder.\n\n**Photo** → **Iris-Z Prepare Image** (512 or 1024, as trained) → **VAE Encode** → reference latent → 4 euler steps\n→ **VAE Decode** → **Iris-Z Depth Decode** → `output/depth/iris_z_...`: the depth near bright (as the other depth\ntemplates here), and Iris-Z's colouring, near red and far blue.\n\n## Settings worth knowing\n\n- **Iris-Z Prepare Image, resolution**: auto takes 512 under 0.5 megapixels, else 1024; the photo is never\n  enlarged. The depth comes back at the photo's own size.\n- **Flux2Scheduler, steps**: 4, Iris-Z's setting for depth. More steps do not help.\n- **Random Noise, seed**: the depth hardly changes with the seed.\n- The depth is relative: log depth scaled per picture, not metres.\n- Time: the first run takes about 2.5 minutes, mostly loading 18 GB; then about 10 s a photo.\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models/iris-z-small** (from [speridlabs/iris-z](https://huggingface.co/speridlabs/iris-z), folder `Iris-Z-small`, revision 5d35ec0)\n\n- transformer-00001-of-00004.safetensors to transformer-00004-of-00004.safetensors (18.2 GB, bf16)\n- empty_prompt.safetensors (13 MB)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein/resolve/main/split_files/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors) (336 MB)\n\n## Where this workflow comes from\n\nOur own graph. Iris-Z is Speridlabs' FLUX.2 Klein base 9B trained to make a picture and its depth map together\n(arXiv 2611.16010). This pack's `iris_z_nodes.py` runs it on ComfyUI core's FLUX.2 model and sampler, written anew\nfrom the Iris-Z SDK (Apache-2.0); one model call matches the SDK's to bf16 rounding. The weights are under the FLUX\nnon-commercial licence: fine for personal and teaching use, not for commercial use. No licence to accept first."
      ]
    }
  ],
